# 8-to-3 Encoder using Verilog HDL

## Overview

This project implements an **8-to-3 Encoder** using Verilog HDL.

An encoder converts one active input line out of eight into a 3-bit binary code.

---

## Inputs

- `D[7:0]` – Eight input lines (only one input should be HIGH at a time)

## Outputs

- `Y[2:0]` – 3-bit encoded output

---

## Truth Table

| Input (D) | Output (Y) |
|-----------|------------|
|00000001|000|
|00000010|001|
|00000100|010|
|00001000|011|
|00010000|100|
|00100000|101|
|01000000|110|
|10000000|111|

---

## Files

- `encoder.v` – Verilog module
- `encoder_tb.v` – Testbench
- `simulation_output.png` – Waveform
- `README.md` – Documentation

---

## Simulation

Compile:

```bash
iverilog -o encoder encoder.v encoder_tb.v
```

Run:

```bash
vvp encoder
```

View waveform:

```bash
gtkwave dump.vcd
```

---

## Expected Output

```text
Input D         Output Y

00000001        000
00000010        001
00000100        010
00001000        011
00010000        100
00100000        101
01000000        110
10000000        111
```

